keywords:
  - cryptographic API misuse
  - LLM code review
  - indirection
  - false positives
  - secure twins
  - balanced accuracy
abstract: >
  Supplement to the preprint "Does Indirection Hurt? Paired Evidence on LLM Review of
  Indirectly Written Cryptographic API Misuse". 90 matched pairs of Python snippets
  (vulnerable and secure twin) in plain and indirect forms, the audit list of 33 pairs
  that are not clean matches, all per-call results (16 open models, 3 repeats) and the
  scripts that recompute the paper's numbers.
